Some days ago I lost a good character (was starting to look for
the vibrating square when I realized that my bell was cursed; no
way to remove the curse...eventually died a stupid death...:-( ).
But this gave me an idea: maybe for a chaotic character the bell
and/or the book really should be cursed for getting into the
sanctum.  Does this make sense?
And since it's easier for a chaotic to escape from Gehennom with
the Amulet, maybe it should become a little harder to get into the 
sanctum...or is this too unbalancing? I guess you COULD have a
hard time trying to find a potion of unholy water...but then,
I think, those potions really should be made more common down
there.
A related idea: a lawful char playing around with a cursed bell
in the valley of the dead SHOULD be punished in some way, imho.
And yes, I like the idea of making the different combinations
(class + alignment) really different; at the moment, once you're
ready to enter Gehennom, it doesn't matter if you're a lawful
priest, a chaotic priest, a cavewoman or an elf...
Any comments?

